0CttCnBlaTK7yOAGuSaAatGnmgpv-uAlPl0Qa4lPMe6Lo_WYy6nr0O17JjqYOrAdhNhool79CAkpFwo0AiBWYYC-vkGaXXnOMU4f0Hiv7HaNNw-rIw\";i:5;s:494:\"places/ChIJv7wdwFj5vDMRkR7VzLalSxM/photos/AVoNoXTYf1TNUhzHM8v7j7G8cZMPhgGNclE7XhecIfZ-HKrYJi9P_-kVOIqtbu3nfuNs52actSToVJkr1yy3PeY4_mBJX0AkZiao7UO6G_c_0pddyzATS1li89tVRzcf1vPEHXNZxj-jW-g2vlTwKeXbhPUI6WErEH2bA5KY48vFzPnqctW95EXVizMclrlJA9y0wnTjriRXpIFZ_8AtTBknurpdBke6SgmN_hKhsEBtOcdWZDBWGu9O5QlHvRQOGhp8mXyXdR_MR9IiD8MYxpIqPrmMrqXXB1b86Uo0U5ABe1yoz32Im40mZSG3Hx2HRc8AgmR7wehayIUl9Hg_RAOGo588JS59Mk1ZqlYIXT5zUQCJL4M10xASxIw4OsGaSLjmbhfsoQn0_ih8Mo3HZQbAbFxPTkr0rVCO3XJ8etUbpjrp2H52Un2brrxri-Uk7f4I\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"vanessa dela cerna\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:119:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWC1O0aYHdKO3IoMT0xEbnPqF0LWi65FH2NEoCduI-dPwY1fyFq=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:584:\"The place is absolutely beautiful, but there are jellyfish around. Especially at Muelle Bay, near their “Little Boracay” area. They can sting and irritate your skin, although fortunately, they were only baby jellyfish.\n\nThere are vendors selling sea urchins there for ₱100 each, but we were offered 3 pieces for ₱200.\n\n**Tip:**\nIf you\'re traveling from Calapan Port to Puerto Galera, it\'s better to travel at night to avoid being approached by people asking for payments. At the border entrance or archway of Puerto Galera, there are personnel collecting an environmental fee.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-09T15:04:32.306285225Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:24:\"Roxanne Joy Diaz (Roxie)\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXMCi0OvvEgJGw0sSvtSXdn2IQlCYjkeq8wuuEaBt6bPxEfsH2L=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:177:\"I stayed in Aninuan and on my way to White Beach I came across this overlooking viewpoint. You can see White Beach in its entirety. Of course i had to stop and take a snap. ?\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-09-12T05:36:26.516788585Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:23:\"Michael Allen Celestial\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU1DDMoi9p6f7LL7E7l_xuuTm36N6oWEOFVoR2iBaqxISvf1M6K=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:73:\"You can utilize the nearby shortcut from Playa Blanca to the White Beach.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2024-04-27T07:49:56.910391Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Traveling Man\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW3d8mAJgymQGI1bR8b4rFz_LoJgDvz1KN-9PqQtyqftucheVOp=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:47:\"Gotta luv it with birds eye view of White Beach\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2023-11-03T01:21:18.259008Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Waldo Smyth\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXQrX1yVRwAObM21MRvlH_PD59oWnWU0JuBzOYekYijd6QK7zE7=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:288:\"Nice place to enjoy the view over White Beach and stairs down to the beach. And it is free. You won\'t get harassed by people trying to sell things.\nOnly downside: traffic right behind you and at times idling cars with silly tourists who stop, roll down their windows to get that snapshot.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2022-11-21T07:55:47.599045Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}}',1788935145),('laravel-cache-rapidapi_search_59e744d6fa396b357528bc8cf03e390d_15.513_120.567','a:20:{i:0;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJN0X9HAC9ljMRoRgabLqnpq0\";s:4:\"name\";s:34:\"Viewpoint – Monasterio de Tarlac\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.436714199999999;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.4303286;s:7:\"address\";s:48:\"CCPJ+M4P, Lubigan, San Jose, Tarlac, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:3:\"poi\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:1;s:7:\