KNrsSRr1LgIkkMD6VHoobB8x1ZKglRMUDIzwCybxMjcCN2exRtQSJKKQBcobf7rWTnlAi6DInO_dNA4ycQKC6WV1KKSfdlMHY2RY-whHcAiXdBdmA8MjzGxvACmbST9MtiUkr-9bfYH2sHQS8AsbuqsvdrOiF7vZvsNM26QA7c5Nn_ea8gKN6klOlMl4yBT1cEhIZUoBaJ5zD2z_FW33qqI3fM5yTxPbxC_p35OQQ47dBCQ63vPBaz9r3ysQYAzMv1yuYIxbS0CmZPNkRx6_VAYr9Vs_PU1-avzF3sFg-IXskwRESOlrCm4cgaH4dNkhFK8RHnwPtySVoFWcb1Yg7aQ0ZHM555UqMQ\";i:5;s:478:\"places/ChIJmx35gBZ_kDMRoSoptxmJUdo/photos/AVoNoXQfU6Fxm5loZW387CgXa7a9ggz-ucaTuza9VKQPtLHn0uTUNkJ3aSwddEgETIrgwZgUDa98Jv_mllOIB-Ofo041E2_ckuNBJPfhH06h9U7ME_qVjrWKjcAW-kZEgqb1Zoui6s5u3z-Ua4B_3IsJJA083S16lZoJLG7GLn20me4SpURExUWo9DnY4DA7if97WtuRTVZfVau_5_UUyjXlmZiyW92K8wvioIpE5fxaun-RNmIbE1VSc5D3C0I6V1Fh8lR2B8G_j-dmBrK7-_b4P3eSSz1aGkpTnYZ05HE7FHfjZCYh3r7XqlUv8qK9xRfy6-7ShE02a7S4bZyAO3srm1j-PtsVsRBY_TrSRBze4otuOAs-3JKP1MYXP489v9NzuWzb5udQDKiCQNYmwjiPEUOnzVZ1DJaY8cEr6dMr36bP3qi1\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Tinee Bee\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUEwFYgoPBFQqANujFWPUXKlAil5EYu543CrUE987uQOd7pciYN_g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:301:\"Great place to see when in Quirino Province. The best time to go is early in the morning for a good hike up the mountain. Awesome view from the top. Breathtaking view of the mountain ranges, the river and the winding road. Not much flowers at this time. Perfect time to visit is November, so they say.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2023-04-18T12:37:50.043443Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:14:\"Andoy Espinosa\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocK4YDdTKFFmeDfdB7YqZU494IMw385iWeWa1nrlWw9JZG_onw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:430:\"Once we entered Nagtipunan Municipal Road, we were treated with breathtaking views of mountains and hills covered with corn crops/plants. The road leading to Landingan Viewpoint is quite steep particularly the last few Kilometers. There is an entrance fee which I assumed is for the maintenance. The only had a few flowers/plants when we visited but the view was awesome! Definitely a place to visit if you\'re in Quirino province.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-03-06T09:28:42.290733Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:14:\"Edmart Fajardo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWboSD9Cddb1W7uAGhzLEmXD3wH1yCtW5AGGR2CJgpDK0_vV8ZM=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:249:\"The place is nice though we came here with few flowers and the plants are just planted. However, it\'s nice and peaceful the view is still picture-worthy. I\'m not sure if it\'s as peaceful as it were during cold season where the flowers bloom the most\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2024-04-01T06:18:58.680458Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:20:\"Maria Isabel Bugtong\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjViTVye84OFSlVzVyINZAqD9qqxOeqqwoRo-1NBnt3x6QkODAI5=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:632:\"Landingan Viewpoint is one of the well known attractions in Quirino. It’s a privately owned property with minimal entrance fee of 50 pesos.\n\nNot sure of its elevation above sea level, but it’s definitely high! This then gives you a very good chance to capture the beautiful scenery! ?\n\nIf you’re into flowers, it might not be the best viewpoint during your visit as the visitors might not know of their planting season, but the view going to Landingan viewpoint is one of the best ridge views I have seen in North Luzon.\n\nI really recommend to take the route going to this Viewpoint! Literally one of the best! ???\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-05-13T16:04:41.325633Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:6:\"Kenjie\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVZI_HZoHRoMZk2HF9wLm2mPpLGfnCzIqduIKbe3qrkShzwJhw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:652:\"Landingan Viewpoint offers some of the most stunning panoramic views of the Sierra Madre mountain range and the winding Cagayan River. The rolling green hills are incredibly picturesque.\n\nThe area is well-maintained, and there are beautiful flower gardens that make for perfect photo spots. There are also viewing decks, cottages, and local vendors selling refreshments and snacks.\n\nTip: The best time to visit is early in the morning to catch the sea of clouds and avoid the midday heat, or late afternoon for a beautiful sunset. The road going up is steep but completely paved and accessible. Highly recommended if you are exploring Quirino Province!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-21T13:58:23.267421626Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:4;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJC4p7SAAPkTMRyuSR7jXJ6A0\";s:4:\"name\";s:9:\"Viewpoint\";s:3:\"lat\";d:16.2267032;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.65269800000002;s:7:\"address\";s:38:\"6MG3+M3P, Itogon, Benguet, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:1;s:7:\"reviews\";i:1;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:476:\"places/ChIJC4p7SAAPkTMRyuSR7jXJ6A0/photos/AVoNoXS0_GcvBeHtgFNb6gplul5gVpHUVtutq_k40fxvWJKgZNxteb6NHmhH1t4ERO__EXcI_FRYvx81LZihaiGkiLBih_ActFyy5rsXaRgj_Vxd9MfB40E6JhN-zGqYeq3RZodG63hyE1I-qsjwcRcPqn6c5yu7gYb35AtJLIXkm5IUGzfDeUftzHr2ZysI4-higT3ZH8IJKzh_A8Ly48VIXwZLLwzeF7h0LO0VNH00IFe3rBK9Tky0NisiSinoKWWTUAV9HB4_qhdsWrWOUr0cMI7JrBGcYQVVSCo8bTvPurwTbg0JvoT0g2dqQLkMjELsDxzEjG6D2bmb5akz_u8P4Ls-RCFJWQZDfS_q0ie_ag_rpn5Y8F5XJeq2xn4mZmd9ahH7bb3R0ev4UASJBhYZU8GNDTeVRD1_d6iMyoqFGeWvTQ\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:3:{i:0;s:476:\"places/ChIJC4p7SAAPkTMRyuSR7jXJ6A0/photos/AVoNoXS0_GcvBeHtgFNb6gplul5gVpHUVtutq_k40fxvWJKgZNxteb6NHmhH1t4ERO__EXcI_FRYvx81LZihaiGkiLBih_ActFyy5rsXaRgj_Vxd9MfB40E6JhN-zGqYeq3RZodG63hyE1I-qsjwcRcPqn6c5yu7gYb35AtJLIXkm5IUGzfDeUftzHr2ZysI4-higT3ZH8IJKzh_A8Ly48VIXwZLLwzeF7h0LO0