zXUhB_bTDRs2LyawawHb3t2j9HYfaLJfjaedXdzMek5pJiKXChg4Y9C-bt8-uC6Hix2u8SAX2ER2Lp4sLkBSSFoCu4CmjG9KTNgzkKHOF6qnYFBCDhZEe372Hbe-I0cTGDJ01oLzu3sEFE_vo1PumdsJ3_rXYX7MaXr0snY4DGdjwHE-qDSHJsRjy1tX52RpbtYDAoWW_M7JuCfOxsnrQeRuL-25weTYcje\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:23:\"Marge Villaester Castro\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjULT33ddaUt9-fABVscikTJiXsj2Y1zBJIsdQBpwkv7VCNFJam28w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:949:\"Disappointing experience at Kusina Food Hall in Petron TPLEX Southbound. Says they’re pet friendly but they’re not.\n\nAte here with our 4 dogs last weekend. We asked first if pets are allowed and they said yes. 2 of our dogs don’t have diapers so we even went back to our car to put their diapers.\n\nWe were reminded twice that dogs are not allowed on the seats and tables (which is truly understandable and normal), we know this because we eat out with our dogs a lot.\n\nBut while we were eating, staff were watching us and circling around us like our dogs would do something wrong.\n\nWe were very uncomfortable so my tito rushed eating so he can take 2 of our dogs outside.\n\nIf you don’t like pets inside your facility, don’t say pets are allowed. We would’ve understood and ate somewhere else.\n\nFood selection is good though! Hopefully pet policy will improve over time. Super dami din langaw, so hopefully they will improve that as well.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-17T02:18:40.419880117Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Yajitra Rik\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVgcclZ4442fZqbpPkWv-g6owthF8ybuCgwaXWl8Eh4_5_g6rY=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:100:\"A convenient place to stop -gas Station, restrooms, foods, or just rest from the trip.\nWide parking.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-17T04:39:07.588417106Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Lance Albo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUYJKYmp6Kiluorf3B58H7wBMkY2PfP1LSfULrA_bl3IYoCXfgh-w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:453:\"This is the only gas station in TPLEX (Tarlac - Pangasinan - La Union Expressway) in both boundaries, I hope more lots that can be equipped to have more gas stations nearby along the expressway for a more convenient travelling experience especially if you\'re bound to Manila or Baguio.\n\nThe gas station itself is large enough especially many parking spaces. Some shops and fast food chain restaurants are available and accessible to choose for you with.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-01-31T09:24:28.128695722Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Alecx Rumbaoa\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjX0RzQs0vdJGeTFBYICunfsK_Mc7PZaIPYMzV6xyZIY8AUluBb2=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:238:\"There are currently 2 ports for EV charging. Just look for the guard before you start plugging in. The charging station is just a few meters away from the restaurant and Petron Station itself. This is in the back side of Kusina Food Hall.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-07T07:40:51.611386080Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"John Ablaza\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVbeKm5reXeoTs3PsrjLre95VDQqrxKo76u_NWUUbFo-ZZlp6e7=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:906:\"A constantly-expanding stopover. I remember when literally only Petron and their restroom was all there is here.\n\nAs of this writing there\'s now a Treats shop, Jolibee, Mcdonalds, Pancake House, Starbucks, and a food hall. There\'s even a Chowking currently under construction.\n\nParking space is plentiful especially on the further part of the stopover.\n\nThis is SMC-owned so of course there\'s only Petron in both North and Southbound parts.\n\nThe first improvement that I could think of that the management should take seriously is ADD TREES. From midday to late afternoon this whole place can feel very hot and dry due to the lack of shade anywhere. Even walking from your car to the stores can make you reach out for your water right away.\n\nOther stopovers don\'t feel this hot and dry due to them being either very compact, or they\'re situated near residential homes where there is plenty of trees around.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-13T05:52:41.453023237Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:9;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJQ9cEZuvHljMRtb0DR6ZTx4o\";s:4:\"name\";s:26:\"Triple 88 Gasoline Station\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.488689099999998;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.54588940000001;s:7:\"address\";s:56:\"Zone 2, Barangay Care,, Tarlac City, Tarlac, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:11:\"gas-station\";s:6:\"rating\";d:2.3;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:4;s:7:\"reviews\";i:4;s:15:\"photo_reference\";N;s:16:\"photo_references\";a:0:{}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:4:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:20:\"Cristina C Dela cruz\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:116:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLf-z6myhzkgugYzpXok-mxo09O8GdQ5HKVGf7WvhM-mryoxg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-02-22T16:28:36.775924Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:7:\"Jin Yap\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUvGY0UlhhBwA-yjXDNYEZzuNULy-xvEJsR2RoMI_6QTps4hcZJtA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:24:\"2018-05-23T05:40:46.096Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:22:\"Graham Russell Mallari\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJQmguOQ1a5Ps2-o05n7kFg3rirj2jNsA62pk-fb3AazV4L6g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:2;s:4:\"text\";s:0:\"\";s: