ec7hhaxX3dRz8rfkVHned7gxF5yWRv1hXmE9IOdIrKHc3y4Gz1olGRzuPcW_D8oLT7lYPpG7xpoyoLGK_B0baRwd5WLxJ0hxfpRNYvtR-lQ\";i:4;s:478:\"places/ChIJ1abFKYXLlzMRLFUriVPw1cs/photos/AVoNoXSkIU6I3NheaxfyJoSh-P-aUgYyoTjjv4_ueLyddiM9VbQLdE6WqEBwr3ElMdkkGYyzQGpqSDVyKFxySRw-tyLSchnHv95Loe42N-PY_jiio26yiALxmMBKWY97x76ZPt92BCZsPPzWkM5HqQ6bOxnn8q4aQzsC-3orJF-6hT7rFp5XYT4lu5C8JV9DsN9zvNxK8nVqTXfcQK8WvN95ufc1U8uF748mOMHYHDGvkBvUPo6c3c4lfG5no_7Ygb-FJ1Ma0OBxQqOIBH3j-v4543mdRcOcifvMhgqwouk5w8JWivP97efWQrIw9W85j8Pj0fWm9mBDrzIudKqfRm-1qz7HDQ-YyR8rwQKCzb4Vvj8bXnpALCliPGZGWevlwfkaDDhfvvQy8tnSpNdgrPiE1ETtyLVNmMIAm4uGnWI3tNAEl-FZ\";i:5;s:476:\"places/ChIJ1abFKYXLlzMRLFUriVPw1cs/photos/AVoNoXRMtFzpaM71hRat886MgGG-lm2-HlVkHJeRxGJnI4KAMdxsW_N-24lvTkY50A3nO70WTtqlxH_i8ktIjf7msEQ2wweUdfJukiDNvka8jtw2mP9C4uWN1GGBHjzS7xTa6EhSG5ISpitHmP3k0bM0e1UPkmjXTMWDIPH4iPtpUKpK1DdecTryc5Vyni6_uuCpSIiFFWVM67N4ozKIQxxBo-z4ddwyBvMaCjgODgQdNWlfCaO2NtyykAebA76cUhSSEuyC1ZJ0tYh1eOBgR9rQf3ZlLbQTicP3PKze4RMO8LHz4k-ga1NTPrTvLvoEWpqo-xDGGqJXnC3pCv6oz38Uar0iVddQgzMzucNYwSe1E147TPJ_qnmqkrij6mYro_YHh9ESaE0Zm1b1_hDGEHKF3TBmA6C8Xj-DFuRcmZZqXjE_CA\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Roland Palaypay\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVjcMhhX_3yHWUYaf_a6Q1rh8auLkShSu0Ay1lA8lN2usRltYLRhQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:771:\"Pasig River Esplanade is a lively place to experience a different side of Manila, especially in the evening. The area is busy and energetic, with plenty of people walking around, enjoying the atmosphere, and taking in views of this part of the city.\n\nThere were several food stalls and vendors that looked very good, though we didn’t end up trying any during our visit. It definitely adds to the nightlife feel of the area.\n\nOne downside is that the river still has a noticeable smell, even though it’s clear there have been efforts over the years to clean it up. That said, the esplanade itself is a nice place to walk around and observe the city’s activity at night.\n\nOverall, a good spot to see a lively part of Manila and take in the atmosphere along the river.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-05T02:57:16.485168266Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"williak belo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUD-kD_iUSkUMTirILZ5ZgbA8LmwU5zOSjALA82glvQ-dacwiA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:529:\"Visited this place on evening with my family. Nice place to visit, we enjoyed it. There is a Rizal mascot on the entrance, and there are guards that maintained security\n\nThough the river smells something but it is something to be improve as well as the lighting and the stretch of the whole esplanade\n\nThe toilets were clean tho the men\'s section was under maintenance.\n\nThere are also independent photographer that will capture your beautiful pose and can print it out immediately\n\nOutside, you can ride tricycle or taxi easily.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-01T17:42:48.430304493Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Karen Antonio\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUPwPSWkEwRDyFSQaRNQCZKdvTflT28re70Pg35Cjb2EMWpcPbX=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:2;s:4:\"text\";s:523:\"beautifully designed and offers stunning views, especially around sunset and in the evening. It’s a great place for a leisurely walk, relaxing, or taking photos. However, the experience was unfortunately affected by the strong smell coming from the river. The odor of stagnant water was quite noticeable and took away from what could have been a much more enjoyable visit. I hope efforts continue to improve the river’s condition because the esplanade itself has so much potential and is truly a beautiful public space.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-28T18:38:27.955647605Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:16:\"Ednhil Almodovar\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWr0IjFgcJHjEAw5qNuapzoEUXqRFyeV_sRg9yYEXpPOXqdYs1u=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:1315:\"I’ve been to Intramuros many times, and I’m so happy that we finally have an esplanade like this. It’s such a good addition for tourism and for locals too. The area feels open, walkable, and safe and a place where you can actually enjoy the Pasig River view and the Walled City skyline at the same time.\n\nIt honestly reminds me of the riverside promenades in Bangkok along the Chao Phraya River. It gives that same relaxing vibe where people can stroll, take photos, or just unwind by the water. This is the kind of public space Manila has needed for a long time.\n\nI really hope the project gets extended so the esplanade becomes longer. It would be amazing if the other side of the river is developed the same way too, with strong cooperation between the Pasig and Manila LGUs. Imagine both banks connected and revitalized.\n\nIt would also be great to see river tours or ferries in the future using this as a main stop that could link Intramuros, Binondo, Makati, and etc. That would boost tourism and transport options at the same time.\n\nMost of all, I hope the cleanliness and proper maintenance of the place will be consistently executed. A beautiful esplanade only stays beautiful if it’s cared for. But overall, this is a big step in the right direction for the Pasig River and for Intramuros. ??\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-29T00:28:17.128034039Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:5:\"Cobie\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUTgQGzSvCrD83zXhmEIBj4FXud2w0TX96iTz6AhoGPAoVPgq8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:633:\"A beautiful place to visit, especially if you just want to relax and enjoy the view. The area is clean, peaceful and perfect for walking around or spending time with friends and family. It becomes even more stunning at night. The lights reflecting on the river create a calming and romantic atmosphere. It’s a great spot for photos and quiet moments. There are also a lot of food stalls where you can buy amazing snacks and street food. It makes the whole experience even better because you can enjoy good food while appreciating the view. Overall, it’s a wonderful place to unwind, especially in the evening. Highly recommended!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-20T10:31:52.576213449Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:9;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJVxSaAyLKlzMRcl0n6OEMiO8\";s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"Manila City Hall\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.589513699999998;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.98161119999999;s:7:\"address\";s:64:\"Padre Burgos Ave, Ermita, Manila, 1000 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.1;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:2526;s:7:\"reviews\";i:2526;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:476:\"places/ChIJVxSaAyLKlzMRcl0n6OEMiO8/photos/AVoNoXRUy005-gF2bu3sae76u5e2JAMQEqGzgLiycyAa54nEGPq_t5aGCeAP_6ASXQh9X5yx93RzfgI9HNWBqPTw9ofb5C5Di09eM2CHOuHwOAELP8PyZn02YFTquxZiNS47tA86kR5Vb4t7Y9ITZfhUXZ4KSH4c1sD5_m9U7DJmEzZsIM5GawW2Ol8_RsojKNFXj1jseJF19tcD-0beID1b223o6kYaCbqwSfa2XPZnFx8DwXNhPZL3Ay5wJcj5d8e-FSopFTdURvD25pWtbMXbNc6m3ofZ7bfNcLbMH-Ikb1ILywl7L8h7e3T5pEpraTtUYKosRwJzi30eT1_CeVVJdP2b35MU3Ye3I-9qfpJTiErOwdq2oPn2lvFNxREsfn9uN9p7SrTUmfPoV1ROSn-GUlgEOPimrOwdaHpUS64C4N2IQA\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:476:\"places/ChIJVxSaAyLKlzMRcl0n6OEMiO8/photos/AVoNoXRUy005-gF2bu3sae76u5e2JAMQEqGzgLiycyAa54nEGPq_t5aGCeAP_6ASXQh9X5yx93RzfgI9HNWBqPTw9ofb5C5Di09eM2CHOuHwOAELP8PyZn02YFTquxZiNS47tA86kR5Vb4t7Y9ITZfhUXZ4KSH4c1sD5_m9U7DJmEzZsIM5GawW2Ol8_RsojKNFXj1jseJF19tcD-0beID1b223o6kYaCbqwSfa2XPZnFx8DwXNhPZL3Ay5wJcj5d8e-FSopFTdURvD25pWtbMXbNc6m3ofZ7bfNcLbMH-Ikb1ILywl7L8h7e3T5pEpraTtUYKosRwJzi30eT1_CeVVJdP2b35MU3Ye3I-9qfpJTiErOwdq2oPn2lvFNxREsfn9uN9p7SrTUmfPoV1ROSn-GUlgEOPimr