00-cc-rp-mo-ba7\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:747:\"We went here to attend the Japanese Matsuri in Manila, which was sponsored by the Japan Embassy. Although, this concert is a paid event. They sell tickets for P150 and P1000 for VIP. You can purchase tickets online and online. We got ours on site, and there was no queue.\n\nThe concert ground was huge with ample space to sit on the grass. The sound system was great until it broke down. There are several stores for selling stiff and food. There are pocket performances in the biitgs. It was a fun Japanese cultural event.\n\nOutside the concert wall was the street parking which was free. Unfortunately, there were homeless people also on the park grounds, and there was trash everywhere. This really affected the aesthetic and safety of the place.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-05-10T22:23:34.841110Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"greg hermosa\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXPwOP1dLTFBtYXgWSigTKAWKFMQQpAlZYTZDvTvmifICnwJvn8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:141:\"This iconic grandstand became witnessed in the historical National Peace Rally of Iglesia Ni Cristo with 1.8 Million in attendance. 13 Jan 25\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-01-22T06:19:14.678970Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"mai angeles\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVbnxcNWCRH4ngYtuDWbusGanjlD3oFa-8r0lYuF_ljE-_jzFIN=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:144:\"This is where I was able to complete my first 16k run through the Rexona Miler Series. Brough back a lot of memories esp the nearby places. ?\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-01T18:01:23.749773089Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Jirehl John\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVBdtn5BQfbG0phqsOF4TH6fLDReTuWfXQx6wZgyE6hLIt9i1c-7g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:419:\"I used to only see this in TV. A place of gatherings all throughout history. Grand celebrations were held and as well as of the known hostage crisis event. Anyway, place isn\'t that grand in person. Would have been a nice place for a jog if not for the presence of so many homeless people. There is so much trash around, this place is a disappointment for local tourists who wanted to see the beauty of the capital city.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2023-11-20T22:57:26.815427Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"JP Travel Diary\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXe0WlGFHDxhIdNDqHgBNdEQTlwCBuv7yvDcCTWcgyR4eGzvaA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:193:\"This is a historical place and the go to location for government activities like fun run and rallies. The area is located in front of Luneta, adjacent to Manila Oceanpark. I love jogging here .\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-01-26T01:37:21.528404Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:100:\"Landmark auditorium from 1949 hosting rallies, presidential inaugurations & Independence Day events.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:11;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJeWcu0hfKlzMRnYOqfe-gowY\";s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"Manila Cathedral\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.5917422;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.97339210000001;s:7:\"address\";s:76:\"Cabildo, 132 Beaterio St, Intramuros, Manila, 1002 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.7;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:7812;s:7:\"reviews\";i:7812;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:478:\"places/ChIJeWcu0hfKlzMRnYOqfe-gowY/photos/AVoNoXSNQZCWc5BUy1VaAvyxVJv-j6V4LvT8wyFPZ3PMThTkOaEXGVhiZZzK_HXIfEJWk7eT_1Z1kRUc42M8b4pAohPH5fNW4v6YD7uOwj6ataWCsKQ65zM-F552X7QBiZHcxSE4JN3M8hE2P-apDCjVXhklqEZLdG4QVorg1QQsnCmQJYXRP02hwQP9cgYpyfO5mI6P8ehc_0ZeCNxaWiAgD4LL8o-ZsllBpdArPGts-8KiZBtk02_A_HsUxGb