YauVUpswHguemZMONDIxpnpDsTVKdEw__MNVuhz04__Piz2RV3Hb1nRxtVXph44sRWllNLL2oO8ewuYJM2-XXI308O3kgPQbp6inTXddgKnVnuoJGRp2ZXYjGMunEtl3e0RB24BAyYhd-c_kWWT5nE4MsUJtSX7XniE6gpKtuQ\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"Manny Yu\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXg-da5a8zn8eyarfcNq2GYSnijPq0sUNl8cm346u4c6jhtgcg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:787:\"New Manila Zoo\n\nReopened with a fresh, modernized layout, the upgraded features significantly improved, cleaner infrastructure designed around animal welfare and an \"open zoo\" concept.\n\nThe tight, traditional iron cages of the past have been largely replaced with spacious, elevated viewing areas, transparent reinforced glass enclosures and a massive netted canopy for the giant aviary where birds fly freely.\n\nVisitors can now explore designated zones like the Reptile House, the Butterfly Garden, and expanded habitats showcasing white Bengal tigers, African lions & capybaras.\n\n​However there are several empty spaces left behind by the absence of an elephant, hippo and giraffe. Nevertheless an enjoyable two hour nature and animal themed escape in the middle of our urban jungle.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-10T10:29:18.567681971Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"Danzhel Dima\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUS60oR57g_2tuT1daXJnTmYVTTi4sbCh6LRL9bmDh-FkFFPxtJ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:243:\"the place is nice and spacious especially the aviary, they even have a cafe inside. I just feel like there’s need to be more animals inside. I also dont get why u need to take your shoes off when entering the primates (monkey enclosure) area\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-20T18:51:43.964949320Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"Ron Matthew Turing\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:119:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU6UMn5tmLjCaNGolLICX885jHtmnXoV1481K9tRWeaSr5k2Xhw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:392:\"The park is highly organized, paved, and fully wheelchair accessible. The air smells much cleaner now due to a new sewage treatment system. However, long-time visitors will notice that the zoo feels a bit empty. Famous residents like Mali the elephant and Bertha the hippo have passed away. You will still see tigers, lions, and monkeys, but do not expect a massive variety of large wildlife.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-09T09:51:00.276268206Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:6:\"Eric W\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:121:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJoEfKbD1gM577V5rpdGT35oOQgJIRzuZH1ZYRN5R97sRf_JMI=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:555:\"First visit to Manila Zoo since the 1990s and while there are fewer animals now, the zoo seems cleaner and conditions have improved somewhat. It’s still not up to the same standards as the best zoos and you can see pretty much everything in an hour so can only give it 3-stars, but it’s definitely an improvement from the past years when conditions for the animals left a lot to be desired. There are several food and drink options including a cafe next to the aviary. Overall a pleasant enough zoo with lots of green areas but relatively few animals.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-02T07:10:00.168778163Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:4:\"Abby\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXzo2ibvZwc0z1TdWPDHOqJxoPuFtOnRbrc94fOkRKYUBqY40Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:317:\"A nice an lovely place to hangout but don\'t expect much animals. There are lots of birds few of other animals. The Capybaras and turtles are the ones carrying the show here. You can buy tickets in advance online by searching manila zoo website. Overall great experience if you just wanna watch animals do their thing.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-01-23T11:48:02.185187212Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:87:\"5.5-hectare zoo & garden featuring diverse animals in modest, old-fashioned enclosures.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:15;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ3ekUHhrKlzMR9Tn7K6JBUBY\";s:4:\"name\";s:47:\"William A. Jones Memorial Bridge (Jones Bridge)\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.595792099999999;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.97722220000001;s:7:\"address\";s:53:\"Jones Brg, Binondo, Manila, Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.6;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:2075;s:7:\"reviews\";i:2075;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:477:\"places/ChIJ3ekUHhrKlzMR9Tn7K6JBUBY/photos/AVoNoXQc67UNx2iwipB8fEogbZscJ49aFA_F1Lqy0aypqVpbYkCsxcsn0GFXmU54yVEe0nv_MEnfOj-tK5s28-4uBc1fIsT0BCkuENrzeNwZ_9QNDQSbQRp69rvhUgpHfTKo6Ce0fhyrJ8q1sglt9ilEdEu_ghcOykilwz1IpReyU_fgpsslmsg-22G2cctDUtDzBx-i59CHeJEYRn5MjH6F8JHiekdf2gQzRS6cRfyDpxP0i1m1Ur_GzHfiBe7ngtGNPqvrnwDvlxqytyFZeXFx0EnYEPVOlh8cUdrDx6e2W3HDPBB_x2WVdrLoZHrf3R6P1L1GtBhcADv__pFoCcJtsOdm7rn32xiDN208bwEdiJzuUwuhbMhuFAJE05n0XabPQOBnNlFy6rLwYoZpnVjIteDvF_gxPxEcR-69UbB5CireFps\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:477:\"places/ChIJ3ekUHhrKlzMR9Tn7K6JBUBY/photos/AVoNoXQc67UNx2iwipB8fEogbZscJ49aFA_F1Lqy0aypqVpbYkCsxcsn0GFXmU54yVEe0nv_MEnfOj-tK5s28-4uBc1fIsT0BCkuENrzeNwZ_9QNDQSbQRp69rvhUgpHfTKo6Ce0fhyrJ8q1sglt9ilEdEu_ghcOykilwz1IpReyU_fgpsslmsg-22G2cctDUtDzBx-i59CHeJEYRn5MjH6F8JHiekdf2gQzRS6cRfyDpxP0i1m1Ur_GzHfiBe7ngtGNPqvrnwDvlxqytyFZeXFx0EnYEPVOlh8cUdrDx6e2W3HDPBB_x2WVdrLoZHrf3R6P1L1GtBhcADv__pFoCcJtsOdm7rn32xiDN208bwEdiJzuUwuhbMhuFAJE05n0XabPQOBnNlFy6rLwYoZpnVjIteDvF_gxPxEcR-69UbB5CireFps\";i:1;s:473:\"places/ChIJ3ekUHhrKlzMR9Tn7K6JBUBY/photos/AVoNoXQBVCuw6Zu9JDJ6TZI_wzyY5Dnp-7Nu6xj0zTNoMh4XVvjeE92ggjeUldypeCnV0kRPW-ttvP8o0tiu0bT-sTFA5qnXYvwvr7kYVR70wh-Es4aexSa8QyWi8yBQknR2gBiaC3AoBpq0q-BOYg95SBZR33U8NFPDiWi8u3kOcykhHV8FY-3Tu8zoOFeCswvKidza9CH_x7PVfDiGjqmEsm34Tr